# =========================================================================
# agnosai — the binary's entry point.
#
# Parity oracle: rust-old/src/main.rs
#
# **Bite 16, the last of M6's transport tier.** `server/serve` connects the
# router to a socket; this is what decides *which* socket, with what state, and
# reads the environment the oracle reads. Until it landed, `./build/agnosai`
# printed `agnosai ready` and exited, so `agnosai_serve` was tested but never
# called by anything.
#
# ## Four things in the oracle have no counterpart here, and none is an omission
#
#   1. **`http_client`** (`main.rs:100-103`). `reqwest::Client::builder()
#      .timeout(30s).pool_max_idle_per_host(10)` has nothing to construct:
#      outbound HTTP goes through `agnosai_guarded_fetch(arena, ...)`, which
#      takes a per-request arena and no client handle (`src/server/state.cyr:21`).
#      The 30 s timeout survives as `AGNOSAI_SERVE_CALLBACK_TIMEOUT_MS`.
#   2. **`let app = router(state)`** (`main.rs:118`). Routing is compile-time
#      dispatch here; `agnosai_serve_mount` is its counterpart and `serve` calls
#      it (`src/server/serve.cyr:307`).
#   3. **`tracing_subscriber::fmt().json()`** (`main.rs:69-72`). sakshi has no
#      JSON output mode and no `EnvFilter`, so no formatter is configured and
#      lines emit as plain text on fd 2 at sakshi's default level. Log
#      *content* matches the oracle line for line; log *transport and format*
#      diverge, which is the honest way to state it.
#   4. **`definitions: DashMap::new()`** (`main.rs:116`). Built inside
#      `agnosai_app_state_new` (`src/server/state.cyr:66`), not passed in.
#
# `with_graceful_shutdown` + `shutdown_signal()` (`main.rs:130`, `:137-153`)
# **used to be a fifth** and no longer is: impossible on sandhi 1.9.8 (ADR 012),
# implemented here once cyrius 6.5.6 vendored sandhi 1.9.9's stop flag. `main`
# installs a `signalfd` SIGINT/SIGTERM handler and drains — see ADR 013.
#
# ## Nothing in this file is `.tcyr`-reachable
#
# The lines at the foot run `main()` at include time, so a suite that included
# this module would start a server. That is why the one piece with a real
# silent-divergence risk — the `u16` port parse — lives in
# `src/server/serve.cyr` as `agnosai_serve_parse_port`, where it is tested,
# while the env plumbing below stays module-local. Acceptance for this bite is
# a live run.
#
# ## `127.0.0.1`, not `localhost`
#
# The oracle defaults `HOOSH_URL` to `http://localhost:8088` (`main.rs:79`);
# `agnosai_hoosh_default_url` answers `http://127.0.0.1:8088`
# (`src/llm/hoosh.cyr:91`). Keep the numeric spelling: sandhi's resolver
# consults no `/etc/hosts` and has no `localhost` special case, so the name
# would take the DNS path and fail on any resolver that NXDOMAINs it. The wire
# target is identical on every conforming host.
# =========================================================================

# Stdlib auto-included via cyrius.cyml

include "src/units.cyr"
